 "seesTitle": "What Sa Foradada sees",
 "seesHTML": "The Son Marroig mirador hangs 230 m over the pierced-rock peninsula with open sea across the whole descent: totality at \u22482.5\u00b0 and the crescent visible to \u224820:49 \u2014 among the longest of any rated spot, thanks to the elevation. Roadside estate parking on the Ma-10; the sunset here is a postcard clich\u00e9 for good reason, and eclipse evening will not be a secret.",
 "capHTML": "Horizon panorama from Sa Foradada: terrain silhouettes with projected angular altitudes against the sun's descent. The crescent is last visible at \u224820:49.",
 "recoTitle": "Around Sa Foradada",
 "recoHTML": "<li><b>The estate mirador</b> \u2014 parking, terraces, the classic Foradada frame.</li><li><b>The peninsula path</b> \u2014 walking down to the rock adds foreground but costs the return climb in the dark.</li><li><b>Port de Valldemossa</b> (10 min E) \u2014 same horizon, smaller crowd, less parking.</li>",
 "verdictText": "Full show \u2014 totality, then the crescent sets into the sea at \u224820:49"
